#edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{4}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186067579 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186067579 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b510294a-158b-59cf-9325-faaa6db5c999" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186067580 #edb/ref 1080 "1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186067580 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186067580 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b70392a5-b997-5c61-a383-809b3402a781" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186067581 #edb/ref 1080 "4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186067581 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186067581 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "547cd2d2-426a-5ed4-ba68-b0d437d86899" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068580 #edb/ref 1069 "e-497" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068580 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{\\ln^2{x}}{x} \\textrm{d}x$ using integration by parts." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068580 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5b83575b-9674-5dc5-b3eb-a918f145be93" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068580 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we let\n\n$$\nI = \\int \\dfrac{\\ln^2 x}{x} \\, \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nTo use integration by parts, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={ln}^{2}⁡x & \\,⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x} & \\,⇒\\,v=\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\int \\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({ln}^{2}⁡x)(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)-\\int (\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)(\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={ln}^{3}⁡x-2\\int \\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={ln}^{3}⁡x-2I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for $I,$ remembering to add a constant of integration $C$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={ln}^{3}⁡x-2I \\\\ 3I & ={ln}^{3}⁡x \\\\ I & =\\frac{{ln}^{3}⁡x}{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068581 #edb/ref 1069 "e-498" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068581 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int e^{x}\\sin{x} \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068581 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "72d0b4b3-bfc6-5339-809f-ff7cd63e4d3a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068581 #edb/ref 1074 "To use integration by parts, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={e}^{x}\\, & ⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\int {e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{x}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-\\int (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)({e}^{x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\int {e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+J.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, we can use integration by parts to evaluate\n\n$$\nJ = \\int e^{x}\\cos{x}\\,\\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nTo do this, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={e}^{x}\\, & ⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the integration by parts formula once more, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}J & =\\int {e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)-\\int (\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)({e}^{x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\int {e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting this back into our equation for $I,$ we can subsequently solve for $I.$ We remember to add a constant of integration $C$ at the end.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+J \\\\ I & =-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-I \\\\ 2I & =-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ I & =\\frac{{e}^{x}}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068644 #edb/ref 1069 "e-7313" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068644 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_0^{\\pi/2} e^x\\sin(2x) \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068644 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f415cae9-6b18-53c1-8c47-6e0a1f0de59c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068644 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's denote the indefinite integral by $I = \\displaystyle \\int e^{x}\\sin(2x)\\, \\textrm{d}x.$\n\nTo use integration by parts, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={e}^{x}\\, & ⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\int {e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{x}(-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2})-\\int (-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2})({e}^{x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\int {e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}J.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, we can use integration by parts to evaluate\n\n$$\nJ = \\int e^{x}\\cos(2x)\\,\\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nTo do this, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={e}^{x}\\, & ⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the integration by parts formula once more, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}J & =\\int {e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{x}(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2})-\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2})({e}^{x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\int {e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, substituting this into our equation for $I,$ we can subsequently solve for $I\\mathbin.$ We can ignore the constant of integration in this case, because it is insignificant for further evaluation of the definite integral.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =-\\frac{{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}J \\\\ I & =-\\frac{{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}I) \\\\ I & =-\\frac{{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}+\\frac{{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{4}-\\frac{1}{4}I \\\\ \\frac{5}{4}I & =\\frac{{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)-2{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{4} \\\\ I & =\\frac{{e}^{x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x))}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate our definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & =(\\frac{{e}^{x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x))}{5}){|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{\\pi /2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2})-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2}))}{5}-\\frac{{e}^{0}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot 0)-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot 0))}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{e}^{\\pi /2}}{5}+\\frac{2}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}({e}^{\\pi /2}+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068734 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049069 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068734 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049332 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068734 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069040 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068734 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069401 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068734 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186250330 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068734 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186250331 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068734 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186250332 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068734 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186319271 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068734 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186319301 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068734 #edb/ref 1039 "Integrating a Logarithmic Expression Using Cyclic Integration by Parts" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068734 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186068580 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068734 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "df0c3b59-7667-53e9-84d3-bba30ea116fb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068735 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050101 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068735 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050271 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068735 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050489 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068735 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050789 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068735 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069068 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068735 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069077 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068735 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186250329 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068735 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186262957 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068735 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186262974 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068735 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186262983 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068735 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186275317 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068735 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186275319 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068735 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186275320 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068735 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186314828 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068735 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186314857 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068735 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186332751 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068735 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding the Indefinite Integral of a Exponential-Trigonometric Expression Using Integration by Parts" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068735 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186068581 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068735 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "b428331b-4916-5b2c-8aa6-89a2358cdef0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068801 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069389 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068801 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069398 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068801 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186319311 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068801 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186319315 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068801 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186323781 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068801 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186323782 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068801 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186332792 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068801 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186332793 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068801 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186351476 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068801 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186351477 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068801 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186351478 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068801 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding the Definite Integral of an Exponential-Trigonometric Expression Using Integration by Parts" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068801 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186068644 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068801 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "d1da25ef-5d1b-588f-b1cc-121562ff98ea" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068957 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186069630 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068957 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186069631 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068957 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186069632 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068957 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186069725 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068957 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068957 #edb/ref 1045 "Integration by Parts in Cyclic Cases" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068957 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186069630 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068957 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048705 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068957 #edb/ref 1050 1500.0 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186068957 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "ad5bc873-c059-5e29-a890-6a3c7109ea97" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069401 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186067576 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069401 #edb/ref 1069 "q-49976" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069401 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_{1}^{e}\\frac{\\ln^{3} z}{z}dz$ using integration by parts." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069401 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d20f7fe1-3115-57de-8eab-3a56c473cbe5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069630 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186069631 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069630 #edb/ref 1061 1752 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069630 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ebba75b0-acff-50bb-8bc5-876149ab4775" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069630 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186070032 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069631 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186069632 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069631 #edb/ref 1061 1753 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069631 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "47b51ee2-f969-5eae-b3ba-5c4a58e33b36" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069631 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186068734 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069632 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186069725 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069632 #edb/ref 1061 1757 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069632 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "08653810-09fe-5a4e-9e3a-e82085484170" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069632 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186068735 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069725 #edb/ref 1061 27070 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069725 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3694456d-b1db-5517-9b35-d043cdc3d3d6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069725 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186068801 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186070032 #edb/ref 1064 "In some cases, applying integration by parts can lead to a cyclic pattern, where the original integral reappears after a few steps. This cyclic behavior allows us to solve the integral by forming an equation that can be solved algebraically.\n\nTo illustrate, let's consider the following example:\n\n$$\nI = \\int \\dfrac{\\ln x}{x} \\textrm{d}x\n$$\n\nLet's try using the method of integration by parts. We suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}x & \\,\\Rightarrow \\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x} & \\,\\Rightarrow \\,v=\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{ln}x\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}x(\\operatorname{ln}x)-\\int (\\operatorname{ln}x)(\\frac{1}{x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={ln}^{2}x-\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}x}{x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={ln}^{2}x-I\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now have the same integral $I$ on both sides of the equality. Thinking about $I$ as some unknown variable, we can easily solve this equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={ln}^{2}x-I \\\\ I+I & ={ln}^{2}x \\\\ 2I & ={ln}^{2}x \\\\ I & =\\frac{{ln}^{2}x}{2}+C\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we added a constant of integration right at the very end of the calculation." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186070032 #edb/ref 1065 904 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186070032 #edb/ref 1066 #u