nt {e}^{2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{2x}(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3})-\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3})(2{e}^{2x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}-\\frac{2}{3}\\int {e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}-\\frac{2}{3}I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting this back into our equation for $I,$ we can subsequently solve for $I.$ We remember to add a constant of integration $C$ at the end.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =-\\frac{{e}^{2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+\\frac{2}{3}J \\\\ I & =-\\frac{{e}^{2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+\\frac{2}{3}(\\frac{{e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}-\\frac{2}{3}I) \\\\ I & =-\\frac{{e}^{2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+\\frac{2{e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{9}-\\frac{4}{9}I \\\\ \\frac{13}{9}I & =\\frac{2{e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-3{e}^{2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{9} \\\\ I & =\\frac{{e}^{2x}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x))}{13}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321729 #edb/ref 1080 "{e}^{-\\pi }+1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321729 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321729 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4a13c3f8-7bec-5eb3-a18e-62df90a347e6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323217 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186321729 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323217 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323217 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323217 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186321729 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323217 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "1926a9f5-5942-57bc-b6e6-d574c97fb17c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323782 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186323217 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323782 #edb/ref 1069 "q-362669" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323782 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323782 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{10}($\n{{field-1}} $)$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323782 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e5475923-10f0-5e28-b504-857701a55831" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323782 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's denote the indefinite integral by  $I=\\int {e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x.$\n\nTo use integration by parts, let's suppose that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={e}^{-x}\\, & ⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-{e}^{-x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\int {e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({e}^{-x})(\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x))-\\int (\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x))(-{e}^{-x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{1}{3}\\int {e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{1}{3}J.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, we can use integration by parts to evaluate\n\n$$\nJ=\\int {e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nLet\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={e}^{-x}\\, & ⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-{e}^{-x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}J & =({e}^{-x})(-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x))-\\int (-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x))(-{e}^{-x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)-\\frac{1}{3}\\int {e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)-\\frac{1}{3}I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our equation for $I,$ we solve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{1}{3}J \\\\ I & =\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{1}{3}(-\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)-\\frac{1}{3}I) \\\\ I & =\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-\\frac{1}{9}{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)-\\frac{1}{9}I \\\\ 10I & ={e}^{-x}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)) \\\\ I & =\\frac{{e}^{-x}}{10}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =(\\frac{{e}^{-x}}{10}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x))){|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =(\\frac{{e}^{-\\pi }}{10}(0-(-1)))-(\\frac{1}{10}(0-1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-\\pi }}{10}+\\frac{1}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}({e}^{-\\pi }+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348752 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{3}{10}({e}^{-\\pi /3}+1)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348752 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348752 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "23815347-d93f-58ba-b1c7-e3ed64d48844" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186349153 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{5}({e}^{-\\pi /3}+3)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186349153 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186349153 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4d7073ff-ed85-58f2-b155-46bd8775ace3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186349666 #edb/ref 1080 "3{e}^{-\\pi /3}+10" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186349666 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186349666 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "8588b43f-4e08-5267-af90-836fa5f9e2b4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186349758 #edb/ref 1080 "2{e}^{-\\pi /3}-5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186349758 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 175921860